vAuth Debian packaging
======================

The canonical Debian metadata is kept in packaging/debian/vauth-0.1.0 so that
other distribution formats and versions can live beside it. Debian tools
require this directory to be named debian at the source-tree root.
build-local.sh creates a temporary clean source tree and performs that mapping
without modifying the checkout.

Static Slint prerequisite
-------------------------

The binary package links Slint statically so installed systems do not need a
Slint runtime package. The local builder must provide a Slint C++ SDK built
with BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF and set VAUTH_SLINT_DIR to the directory containing
SlintConfig.cmake, for example:

  VAUTH_SLINT_DIR=/opt/slint-static/lib/cmake/Slint \
    packaging/debian/vauth-0.1.0/build-local.sh

Slint is intentionally not listed as a Debian Build-Depends while no suitable
Debian package exists. Consequently this initial packaging is suitable for
local beta packages and a controlled project repository, but it is not yet a
self-contained Debian archive source package.

Release blockers
----------------

The three JSON animation documents under client/assets do not yet have recorded
provenance and redistribution terms. Public packages must not be distributed
until those terms are established or the assets are replaced.

A statically linked vauth-ui also incorporates Slint. Public binary packages
must include the exact Slint license and all notices corresponding to the SDK
used for that build. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the project's current
license selection and remaining notice work.
